From: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: mediatek: do not retrain a port limited to Gen1

mtk_pcie_retrain() retrains every root port after enumeration to reach
Gen2. Port 0 of EN7528 has a Gen1-only PHY but still advertises 5 GT/s,
so the retrain attempt fails and drops the link. The endpoint behind it
then resets its configuration space and loses the BARs assigned during
enumeration; the first memory access to it hangs the bus (seen with the
second PCIe interface of an MT7915 on a Nokia G-1426-MA).

Skip the retrain when the host bridge node limits the link to Gen1 with
the standard max-link-speed property.

Signed-off-by: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-mediatek.c
@@ -874,6 +874,15 @@ static int mtk_pcie_retrain(struct devic
 	if (!IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_PCIE_MEDIATEK))
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * A port limited to Gen1 has nothing to gain, and on EN7528 port 0
+	 * (Gen1 PHY, but advertising 5 GT/s) the failed attempt drops the
+	 * link, which resets the endpoint and loses the BARs assigned during
+	 * enumeration.
+	 */
+	if (of_pci_get_max_link_speed(dev->of_node) == 1)
+		return 0;
+
 	guard(rwsem_read)(&pci_bus_sem);
 
 	for_each_pci_bridge(rp, host->bus) {
